  "scope": "Share occupation selector-to-held-tile argument",
  "validation": "Paired target and ArithmeticCellWindow client builds pass with byte-identical client objects. A fresh WholeField provider and four prior direct project providers have source/object receipts. All 70 existing target declaration/type/axiom reports match; one private helper is added. 33,463 default simp and 14,822 instance entries match.",
  "limitations": [
    "Initial WholeField setup failed with a missing Foundation overlay; its log/time survive without a structured receipt. A later baseline client attempt failed because WangStrip was absent; its structured receipt/log/time are preserved. Both issues were corrected before paired builds.",
    "Post-build samples of provider/target search paths resolve a pre-adoption BinaryCarry object, and the historical WindowInterface environment used older HalfBinomial, BinomLegendre and PellRecurrence objects. These are distinct observations; later samples of the Occupation search paths resolve the newer source-matched PellRecurrence. Transitive inputs were not pinned at Occupation build time, so the later sample cannot certify historical bytes or whether every sampled object was loaded.",
    "Other transitive project/Foundation/package objects are cached; no full current-source closure rebuild is established. The client search was limited to tracked exact-import Lean sources, and other clients or environment extensions remain outside the tested scope.",
    "Single paired shared-load timing samples are not a general performance benchmark. Compiled objects are not archived; object hashes and resolution are recorded in receipts, and live external objects are needed for independent byte checks."
  ],
